        "speaker": "client",
        "text": "1\\. Site list\nThe model should follow the Business Case site list.\n\n2\\. Opex figures\nFor the correct program-level operating assumption, apply the CAD 30–40M/year range in the original brief. The Appendix amount appears incomplete or understated and must not be used for the complete network model.\n\n3\\. Availability payment approach\nCalculate the availability payment so that it meets both of these thresholds:\n\n\\- A minimum DSCR of approximately 1.35x, and\n\n\\-bA minimum equity IRR within the 12–15% range. Do not base the model only on DSCR when that produces negative equity returns.\n\n4\\. Program-wide/shared costs\nShow the digital platform, program management, and contingency/reserve as separate model line items. They form part of total program capex and should not be left out.\n\n5\\. Financing structure\nFor now, the simplified 70/30 debt/equity structure at approximately 6% is fine. Mezzanine does not need to be modeled as a separate layer yet; keep the structure streamlined until lenders are engaged, at which point we can refine it.\n\n6\\. Tax/depreciation\nIncorporate CCA/depreciation correctly by applying the standard Canadian Capital Cost Allowance classes relevant to each asset type, such as Class 1 for buildings, Class 43 for clean energy equipment, and Class 8 for furniture/fixtures, among any others that apply. This is critical to a credible government submission and will have a material impact on both the tax shield and equity returns.\n\nThe immediate objective is to produce a coherent base-case model promptly and then refine it through iteration."
